//RS //! Native boundary for compiled-workload peer commands.
//RS //!
//RS //! The launcher deliberately has no ambient fallback. Linux uses Bubblewrap
//RS //! mount and namespace isolation, macOS uses Seatbelt, and Windows uses the
//RS //! repository's AppContainer backend plus temporary Firewall rules for the
//RS //! loopback-only policy.
//RS 
